ex` answers `nil` for numeric keys (so `ipairs`/numeric loops end)\". Its side effect on direct indexing is finding 6. (b) Comparisons, arithmetic and `..` on a stub raised and ended the scan. Now they give false, 0 and a string (lines 214-250); PR: \"degrade to harmless values instead of raising\". (c) `tostring(stub)` gave `table: 0x...`; now it gives an empty string (line 251). (d) The scan had no time limit; now it has 10s (line 90). (e) The cache version was v14; now it is v15 (line 598). (a), (b) and (d) are the PR's stated intent. No test pins (c). None of these is recorded with `proof change behavior-diff classify-inventory`.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":202},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":214},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":251},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":90},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-0W96","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Removed-behaviour inventory (my reading; the engine's inventory is empty)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings:build_lua_bind_cache"],"scenario":"user ~/.config/hypr/monitors.lua builds a mode with string.format(\"%dx%d@%d\", m.width, m.height, m.refresh_rate) from hl.get_active_monitor(); the scan ends before hypr.bindings and the user's binds and rebinds are missing from the menu cache"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"The stub absorbs operators, but library functions check the argument's type and raise without calling metamethods. hyprland.lua requires hypr.monitors (line 19) and hypr.input before hypr.bindings (line 21). So one such line in a user monitors.lua still ends the scan. My runs on the merge with the full shipped config plus a user rebind and bind: `string.format(\"%dx%d@%d\", m.width, m.height, m.refresh_rate)` gives `bad argument #2 to 'format'`. The SSH bind is missing and the Terminal rebind falls back to the default. This is arm B of the KI reproducer (pocs/crs-260930-jvx8-c01.sh line 82). `math.floor(m.width)` and `string.lower(m.name)` behave the same way. A per-module `pcall` around `require` keeps those binds in my runs.","refs":[{"id":"config/hypr/hyprland.lua","kind":"file","line":19},{"id":"pocs/crs-260930-jvx8-c01.sh","kind":"file","line":82},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":296},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-KEYBINDINGS-SCAN-DOFILE-ABORT.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-0W96","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: should a library call on a stub value in a user module still drop every bind loaded after it?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"A user module with a type-checked library call does not drop binds loaded after it\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings:build_lua_bind_cache"],"scenario":"user monitors.lua does `local first = hl.get_monitors()[1]; hl.monitor({ output = first.name })`: under the new stub [1] is nil, the scan raises before hypr.bindings and the user's binds stay missing (on base as shipped they were already lost at qconsole)"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"A numeric key now gives `nil` (line 202), so `local first = hl.get_monitors()[1]; hl.monitor({ output = first.name })` raises `attempt to index a nil value`. On base 1e433732 as shipped, the scan already stopped earlier, at the qconsole comparison (qconsole.lua:123). So for a user with this line the binds stay missing: the PR does not fix them, but it is not a regression against base as shipped. The stub change is what decides the outcome once qconsole is absorbed. My run, with qconsole's comparisons guarded (as reproducer arm B does) and the line appended to the user's monitors.lua: base caches 229 binds, including the SSH bind and the alacritty Terminal rebind. The merge caches 228, without SSH, and Terminal reverts to `omarchy-launch-terminal`. The shipped config has no such index. Guarded forms (`if first then`) and `ipairs` loops are unaffected. A per-module `pcall` around `require` keeps the binds in my run. Our KI note (commit aeae174b) records the same result.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":202},{"id":"config/hypr/hyprland.lua","kind":"file","line":19},{"id":"default/hypr/qconsole.lua","kind":"file","line":123},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-KEYBINDINGS-SCAN-DOFILE-ABORT.yaml","kind":"file","line":22},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-0W96","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Question: an unguarded numeric index on a stub list still ends the scan. Not fixed by this PR; should it be?","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"behavior hazard: settled only by a recorded test outcome","note":"A runtime-behavior question the package's static facts cannot settle; it needs a test. Suggested test: \"An unguarded `hl.get_monitors()[1].name` in a user module does not drop later binds\".","status":"needs_test"}},{"claim":{"params":{"relatesTo":["bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings:build_lua_bind_cache"],"scenario":"user config walks w = w.parent from hl.get_active_window() at load time: the scan runs to the 10s timeout on every cache miss and the menu opens with the binds declared before the loop only"},"type":"behavior_hazard"},"detail":"`timeout 10 lua` (line 90) bounds the scan, so no runaway `lua` outlives the menu: the PR's 27-hour case. A load-time loop the stub never ends still runs to the limit, e.g. `local w = hl.get_active_window(); while w and w.parent do w = w.parent end`. My run on the merge: the scan is killed after 10.0s (exit 124). The bind declared before the loop is 