 base as shipped. This assessment is advisory only."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":5,"rationale":"Append to menu-keybindings-lua-scan-test.sh. hyprland.lua requires hypr.monitors, then hypr.bindings. monitors.lua does `string.format(\"%dx%d\", m.width, m.height)`. Assert the bind from bindings.lua is reported. It fails on this merge; a per-module pcall around require passes it.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/menu-keybindings-lua-scan-test.sh","kind":"file","line":58},{"id":"config/hypr/hyprland.lua","kind":"file","line":19}],"title":"A user module with a type-checked library call does not drop binds loaded after it"},{"forClaim":6,"rationale":"Same fixture as above, with `local first = hl.get_monitors()[1]; hl.monitor({ output = first.name })` in monitors.lua. It fails on this merge; the per-module pcall passes it.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":202}],"title":"An unguarded `hl.get_monitors()[1].name` in a user module does not drop later binds"},{"forClaim":7,"rationale":"Fixture: a bind, then `local w = hl.get_active_window(); while w and w.parent do w = w.parent end`. Assert the scan returns within ~10s, no lua process remains, and the earlier bind is reported. This states the intended bound explicitly.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":90}],"title":"A load-time loop the stub never ends: bounded wait, earlier binds kept"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #7564 (tobi) fixes the keybindings menu's Lua bind scan, which runs the user's `hyprland.lua` under a stub `hl`. The stub now answers `nil` for numeric keys, so `ipairs` over stub values ends. Comparisons, arithmetic, `..`, `#` and `tostring` give harmless values instead of raising. The scan runs under `timeout 10`, and the cache version goes v14 to v15. A new test (menu-keybindings-lua-scan-test.sh) pins it. On the mirror that is commit 454ad3cd. The later commits are our proof work: a two-arm reproducer, KI notes and evidence, trace re-reviews, a `Verifies:` line on the PR's test, and two obligation tags on existing keycode tests.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** Coverage of the changed file was not measured (coverage_unmeasured): the changed lines are Lua inside a heredoc. The PR's scan test ran in the audit and passed. 69 results were ingested (69 passed, 0 failed). My runs: the scan test fails at base 1e433732 (the scan spins to the 10s limit) and passes 3/3 on the merge. The KI reproducer's shipped-config arm flips; its user-module arm does not.\n\n**Compatibility.** The package says compatible (4 sources, 0 findings). But the differential harness covers only the menu QML/JS files, and the removed-behaviour inventory is empty, so none of this exercises the scan.\n\n**Readiness.** ready under the approved policy, with 4 informational disclosures. The next decision is human_judgement (acceptance), by a maintainer. Nothing in this review is an approval.\n\n**Questions for a human.** (1) A library call that type-checks its argument (`string.format(\"%d\", m.width)`, `math.floor`) in a user `monitors.lua` still ends the scan before `hypr.bindings`. (2) An unguarded `hl.get_monitors()[1].name` also ends it, because numeric keys now answer `nil`. On base as shipped the scan already stopped at qconsole, so for such a user the PR leaves the binds missing; it does not fix them. (3) A config the stub cannot finish now makes the menu wait 10s. A per-module `pcall` around `require` settles (1) and (2) in my runs.\n\n**Traceability.** 0W96 and 9DMS match only at file level. Change effects were not analyzed (effects_unavailable), so the empty spec-gap list proves nothing.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** No gate failed: 178 passed, unchanged from the baseline. 13 were skipped by configuration. The reproducer file is out of scope."}
